Parts of this project adapt logic, regular expressions and word lists from career-ops
(https://github.com/career-ops-hq/career-ops), used under the MIT License:

  - packages/sources/src/liveness.ts: text normalization, closure and apply-control patterns,
    the classification order, and the per-board API rules (liveness-core.mjs, liveness-api.mjs)
  - packages/sources/src/workday.ts: the Workday CXS jobs endpoint and "Posted N Days Ago"
    parsing (providers/workday.mjs)
  - packages/core/src/writing.ts: banned word and phrase lists and the date-range dash exemption
    (cv-voice.mjs, modes/_writing.md, voice-dna.template.md)
  - packages/core/src/voice.ts: the numeric writing-sample measures (writing-profile.mjs)
  - packages/core/src/stories.ts: STAR story fields and the number provenance check
    (lib/story-bank.mjs, story-provenance-check.mjs, verify-cv-facts.mjs)
  - packages/ai/src/outreach.ts: the three-sentence message structure and length cap
    (modes/contacto.md)

The code was rewritten in TypeScript for this project; none of the original files are included.

